WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.039
Week 7: Questions and High-Frequency Irregulars. request specific information state ability and intention repair a misunderstanding

2
00:00:09.039 --> 00:00:15.305
Cultural lens. Directness, softeners, and polite requests in service encounters.

3
00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:27.739
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.739 --> 00:00:39.747
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.747 --> 00:00:48.959
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:48.959 --> 00:01:09.841
Model language. ¿Qué quiere hacer hoy? — What do you want to do today? ¿Cuándo viene el autobús? — When does the bus come? No sé; ¿puede repetirlo? — I don't know; can you repeat that? Tengo que hacer una llamada. — I have to make a call. ¿Por qué dices eso? — Why do you say that?

7
00:01:09.841 --> 00:01:19.995
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
